hushphone (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop the SQLite dependency that came with the thin client's persistent API
    (RUSTSEC-2026-0459).
  * Android: Screen security, an opt-in setting that keeps screens out of screenshots;
    off by default, where 0.2.0 always kept them out.

 -- Katzenpost <packages@katzenpost.network>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:47:01 +0000

hushphone (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Run over a Reticulum mesh as well as the mixnet: --transport mixnet, reticulum (Rust,
    the default build) or reticulum-py; on Android, Settings picks the mixnet or the mesh.
  * Radio mode: received voice messages play as they arrive, on a two-way radio screen.
  * Ping: the bell or Ctrl+P plays a short tone on every member's device.
  * Vouchers shown as QR codes and scanned by camera, webcam or screenshot; sent and heard by
    sound with ggwave, as a T-Deck sends them.
  * A pending-vouchers dialog lists every group still joining and cancels any.
  * --wire-version 3|4, saved in settings; version 4 (compact vouchers) is the default.
  * Show messages this app cannot show in the notice bar.
  * Android: attach and save through the document picker; version codes per ABI.

 -- Katzenpost <packages@katzenpost.network>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

hushphone (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Encrypt the state file and attachments whole at rest, with a random key kept by
    the Secret Service keyring on Linux or the Android Keystore; warn when no keyring runs.
  * Seal an existing plain state in place on first start with a key.
  * Record voice notes into guarded memory, never to a file.

 -- Katzenpost <packages@katzenpost.network>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:04:50 +0000

hushphone (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep the data directory its owner's alone; the process cannot be dumped or traced.
  * On Android, keep the state out of backups and device transfers.
  * Read caps, write caps and voucher secrets in guarded memory, wiped on drop.
  * Use pigeonhole_protocols, now one crate.

 -- Katzenpost <packages@katzenpost.network>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:09:22 +0000

hushphone (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Join through katzenqt voucher replies without rosters, and retry voucher reads that fail.
  * Reopen the client when it stops; cancel a pending join.
  * A seccomp filter in the binary and an AppArmor profile: no IP sockets, no programs.
  * On Android, reach kpclientd through kpclientd-android's connect, with no network.

 -- Katzenpost <packages@katzenpost.network>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:42:26 +0000

